WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.780
Public schools are free to students.

2
00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:06.020
Street lights are free to
everyone who walks under them.

3
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:08.300
Both are paid for by government.

4
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:12.510
But economists say only one
of them is a true public good.

5
00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:15.550
Some goods the market
may not supply at all.

6
00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:20.020
Think of a lighthouse: every
passing ship gains from its beam.

7
00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.560
So if everyone gains from a lighthouse,

8
00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.090
why might no one choose to pay for it?

9
00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:28.170
In this mission, you'll
sort goods with two tests,

10
00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.780
from a sandwich to national defense.

11
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.100
Then you'll put two neighbors in a game:

12
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.330
will either pay for a flood
barrier they both want?

13
00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:39.640
Your mission: find out
why a good everyone values

14
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.090
can be hard to pay for.
